# skyeCladach -- Conall on the shore of Skye
#
# The player's first conversation on the island. Conall, the Warden, keeps the
# green for Uathach (who stays up on her dais until the tournament). He invites
# them up the wall -- no drill, no orders: they find the stair themselves (the
# scene nudges with the brooch if they stall). His lines are captions, not cards
# -- see js/game/scenes/locations/skye/skyeCladach.js. This draft is only what
# he says when you tap him.
#
# NOTES USED
#   climb_started         -> "I'm coming." chosen; he leaves them to the wall
#   climb_top             -> (scene) they're on the top of the wall; opens the pep talk
#   go_loch / go_garden    -> pep-talk choice; one-off, the scene clears it
#   pep_done               -> (scene) the pep talk is over; he goes ahead and is gone
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS PLACEHOLDER -- the structure is the point. Irish is a first draft.
# (The old "onward to the machaire" nodes are gone: once the pep talk is done he has left.)

@file skye/skyeCladach


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — the landing
@continue
So. The sea gave you up.
% Bhuel. Scaoil an fharraige uaithi thú.
I am Conall. I keep the green for Uathach, Scáthach's daughter.
% Is mise Conall. Coimeádaim an fhaiche d'Uathach, iníon Scáthaí.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE PEP TALK -- at the top of the wall, opened by the scene when they
# arrive (climb_top). The subtext is the whole project: you came, and that
# matters. He never says so.
= node 1 — the top
@when note climb_top
@when !note pep_done
@hold
You found the stair.
% Fuair tú an staighre.
Welcome to Skye. Not many come this way. You did.
% Fáilte go Scí. Ní thagann mórán an bealach seo. Tháinig tusa.
There's a garden over west, where I teach the first lessons. Uathach won't come down for those. You'll see her at the tournament.
% Tá gairdín thiar ansin, mar a mhúinim na chéad cheachtanna. Ní thiocfaidh Uathach anuas dóibh siúd. Feicfidh tú í ag an gcomórtas.

* On to the loch.
% Ar aghaidh chuig an loch.
@note go_loch
@exit

* To the garden first.
% Chuig an ngairdín ar dtús.
@note go_garden
@exit


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2 — the invitation
@when !note climb_started
@hold
@again Well? / Bhuel?
The wall is old, and there's a stair in it somewhere. Come up when you're ready.
% Tá an balla seo sean, agus staighre ann áit éigin. Tar aníos nuair a bheidh tú réidh.

* I'm coming.
% Tagaim aníos.
@note climb_started
@exit

* Who is Scáthach?
% Cé hí Scáthach?
@first
> Who is Scáthach?
% Cé hí Scáthach?
< The finest teacher of arms in the world.
% An múinteoir arm is fearr ar domhan.
< And the hardest.
% Agus an ceann is crua.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2a — on the wall
@when note climb_started
@hold
Come up.
% Tar aníos.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE LANDFALL -- the cut-scene that opens a first arrival (landfall.js). The
# scene sets landfall_talk and opens this itself, and clears it afterwards. The
# cards are the player's to read at their own pace. There are no buttons: the
# > / < lines straight under the node are an exchange it plays out, and then
# the conversation closes. The last exchange is NOT here: it is played by the
# scene as captions while Conall drags the champion off (landfall.js, LINES):
#     (player)  I am coming.                    Tá mé ag teacht anois.
#     (Conall)  I see that thou art.            Feicim go bhfuil.
#     (Conall)  There is no need to narrate it. Ní gá é a rá
# This node is last in the file on purpose: the saved npcProgress of anyone
# who has already played the old welcome still points at the same nodes.
= node 3 — the landfall
@when note landfall_talk
@hold
Bright the brow above the oar!
% Geal an éadan os cionn an maide!
Hero's light sits on that forehead
% Solas an ghaiscigh ar an éadain.
Victory walks behind that shoulder
% Gabhann an ghaiscíocht le hais na gualainne sin.

> Long have I rowed, for Skye's grey shore.
% Iomramh fada déanta agam, i gcomhair chladach oileánn an Cheo.
> My back is telling me so.
% Tá mo dhroim féin ag cur in iúl dom é.
< Wilt thou come to the fire?
% An dtiocfaidh tú chois tine?
> I will come to the fire.
% Tiocfadh mé chois tine.
< Then come.
% Tar, mar sin.
